BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
48. 417.8899999999999864 Td
(The System of National Accounts 2008 \(SNA 2008\) is the internationally agreed standard for compiling and) Tj
T* (disseminating national accounts statistics. It was developed jointly by the United Nations, IMF, World Bank, OECD, and) Tj
T* (Eurostat and replaced the earlier SNA 1993.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
48. 370.8899999999999864 Td
(The SNA provides a coherent, consistent, and integrated set of macroeconomic accounts that can be used to analyse) Tj
T* (the performance of an economy, determine economic policy, and make comparisons across countries and over time.) Tj
T* (India adopted the SNA 2008 framework with the base year revision to 2011-12, published in January 2015.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
48. 323.8899999999999864 Td
(The SNA is organised as an integrated sequence of accounts covering:) Tj
T* (- Production) Tj
T* (- Income generation and distribution) Tj
T* (- Accumulation \(capital\)) Tj
T* (- Financial flows) Tj
T* (- Balance sheets \(stocks\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 13 Tf
14.9499999999999993 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
48. 225.8899999999999864 Td
