BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
54. 753.8899999999999864 Td
(The SNA production boundary defines what is and is not counted as economic production. It includes:) Tj
T* (- All market production \(goods and services produced for sale\)) Tj
T* (- Production for own final use \(e.g., subsistence farming, own-account construction\)) Tj
T* (- Non-market production by government and NPISHs) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (It excludes: household domestic services \(cooking, cleaning for own use\), volunteer services, and illegal activities) Tj
T* (\(though these are recommended for inclusion if significant\).) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
54. 652.8899999999999864 Td
(2.3 Asset Boundary) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
54. 637.8899999999999864 Td
(Assets are entities owned or controlled by institutional units from which economic benefits are expected to flow in) Tj
T* (the future. The SNA 2008 expanded the asset boundary to include:) Tj
T* (- Intellectual property products \(R&D, software, databases\)) Tj
T* (- Land improvements) Tj
T* (- Biological resources) Tj
T* (- Financial assets and liabilities) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
54. 549.8899999999999864 Td
(2.4 Residence) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
54. 534.8899999999999864 Td
(Residence in the SNA is determined by the "centre of predominant economic interest" rule-an economic unit is) Tj
T* (resident in the territory where it engages in economic activities for one year or more, regardless of nationality. This is) Tj
T* (distinct from citizenship.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
54. 485.8899999999999864 Td
(2.5 Valuation Principles) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
54. 470.8899999999999864 Td
(SNA 2008 uses consistent valuation principles:) Tj
T* (- Outputs valued at basic prices \(excluding taxes on products, including subsidies\)) Tj
T* (- Uses \(intermediate/final\) valued at purchasers' prices \(including taxes, excluding subsidies\)) Tj
T* (- GDP at market prices reconciles the two via taxes minus subsidies on products) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 13 Tf
14.9499999999999993 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
48. 396.8899999999999864 Td
