(7. Data Quality Considerations) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
48. 618.8899999999999864 Td
(- **Consistency across accounts**: The integrated nature of SNA means errors in one account propagate to others.) Tj
T* (Cross-checking balancing items across accounts is essential.) Tj
T* (- **Institutional sector classification**: Misclassification of entities \(e.g., public enterprises as government vs.) Tj
T* (corporations\) affects the sectoral distribution of accounts.) Tj
T* (- **Valuation**: Moving between market prices and basic prices requires accurate data on taxes and subsidies on) Tj
T* (products, which may be incomplete for sub-sectors.) Tj
T* (- **Financial account reconciliation**: The discrepancy between net lending/borrowing from capital account and) Tj
T* (financial account is a measure of overall statistical quality.) Tj
T* (- **Balance sheet data**: Asset stock data \(especially for produced fixed assets\) requires perpetual inventory models) Tj
T* (and assumptions about asset lifetimes and depreciation patterns.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 13 Tf
14.9499999999999993 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
48. 468.8899999999999864 Td
(8. Key Learning Points) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
48. 450.8899999999999864 Td
(1. SNA 2008 is the internationally agreed framework for national accounts; India adopted it with base year 2011-12.) Tj
T* (2. The SNA classifies resident units into 5 institutional sectors and the rest of the world.) Tj
T* (3. The production boundary defines what is included in GDP; the asset boundary defines what is capitalised.) Tj
T* (4. The sequence of accounts links production through income distribution, saving, and capital formation to balance) Tj
T* (sheets.) Tj
T* (5. Key SNA 2008 changes: capitalisation of R&D, military weapons, and software; improved FISIM; pension treatment.) Tj
T* (6. Consistency across the sequence of accounts is a key quality indicator.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 13 Tf
14.9499999999999993 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
48. 339.8899999999999864 Td
(9. Learning Outcomes) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
48. 321.8899999999999864 Td
(On completing this material, you should be able to:) Tj
T* (- Describe the structure, purpose, and international status of SNA 2008.) Tj
T* (- Identify the five institutional sectors and explain the production and asset boundaries.) Tj
T* (- Trace the sequence of accounts from production to balance sheets.) Tj
T* (- Identify the key changes between SNA 1993 and SNA 2008 and their implications.) Tj
T* (- Apply SNA 2008 concepts to India's national accounts compilation context.) Tj
ET
BT
